From 7baec436f0074c98145f7daeb61cabcac0fdb324 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Mar 2026 23:25:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Remove GrapheneOS features incompatible with GSI

Remove Auditor references from framework:
- Remove app.attestation.auditor from GmcPackageManager HIDDEN_PACKAGES
- Remove bundled Auditor app certificate digest from
  read_additional_security_state_known_signers
- Remove app.attestation.auditor from notification permission grants
Auditor relies on hardware attestation tied to specific device models
and will never pass verification on a GSI.

Disable SELinux flags kernel support notification:
The GSI does not ship a GrapheneOS-patched kernel so the custom
SELinux flags proc attribute will never be present. The framework
already gracefully disables the affected hardening features when the
kernel lacks support, but still posts a persistent notification on
every boot for debuggable builds. Remove the notification since it is
expected and not actionable on a GSI.
